Patch 0010. A study is a photograph; a hall is not. Contracted power moves, tenancy
frees up, the tenant changes platform, a quotation lands. Six months later the
client's question is never "solve it again" — it is "what moved, and why." Nobody
else can answer it, because nobody else is holding the model.

THE CHANGE ENGINE (gridforge/change.py)

    python3 -m gridforge diff was.json now.json -o out
    POST /v1/diff   {before, after} or {previous_state, after}

Attribution is a one-at-a-time contribution analysis: move one input from its old
value to its new one, re-solve, and the change in the answer is that input's
contribution. The note therefore names a CAUSE, not just a delta — "contracted
capacity 12.0 to 10.5 MW: -9 racks" — and flags the inputs that change WHAT BINDS
FIRST even when they add no racks.

What the probes do not explain is reported as a residual rather than distributed.
Constraints interact; two inputs that each do little can matter together, and one
that helps alone can be masked by another. A driver table that silently adds up to
the wrong number is worse than no driver table, and a test asserts drivers plus
residual equal the total.

The comparison is pinned to one scenario in both runs, so a change in the answer is
a change in the hall rather than a change of subject; a change in which architecture
is recommended is reported separately as its own news.

diff_from_state compares a recorded answer against the hall solved today. That is
the case where nothing the client supplied has changed but OUR libraries have — a
quotation replaced a placeholder, a platform's figures were revised. The note says
so explicitly instead of implying the client moved something.

THE CHANGE NOTE (gridforge/reporting/change_note.py)

Four sections, not another study. A subscription that sends fifty pages every
quarter gets unsubscribed; one that names the input that moved the answer gets
renewed. A run that finds nothing material says so in three lines and recommends no
action — manufacturing a finding to justify the fee is how this product would die.

HALL WATCH — EUR 6,000 per quarter

Stripe subscription mode, a watches table, a client page at /watch/<token> that
re-solves immediately on an input update rather than making them wait for the
schedule, a weekly Vercel cron (authorised by CRON_SECRET) that re-runs due halls
against current libraries, and watched halls plus annualised recurring revenue on
/admin/pipeline. The offer sits under every delivered study, which is the honest
moment: they have just read the photograph.

ARCHITECTURE

The selection policy (Objective, pick_recommended) moved from reporting to
scenario/objective.py, and the diff from envelope/ to gridforge/change.py. Reporting
must not be a dependency of the thing it reports on, and the change engine is
orchestration rather than a domain. The architecture test caught both.

Also removes walkthrough_deck_sample.html from the repository root and gitignores
stray patches.

155 Python tests pass, up from 137. tsc, next lint and next build clean.
Migration 0005 adds watches and watch_notes.

